===== STEP 9: this run's (a)(b)(c) summary =====
(a) observed.txt shows exactly the claimed behaviour: text 'h': 0.732612' ; JSON Overall.hAssessed 5.860893744485249 = 8 x hBitstring 0.7326117180606562 (rel 1e-12) ; dataWordSize 8.0 ; -vvv 'H_bitstring Per Symbol = 5.8608937444852494' = 'Assessed min entropy'. Values identical to the author's record; only timestamp/git header lines differ.
(b) control.sh changes TWO things (fixture rand1_short.bin AND declared width 1). Weaker than a one-variable control, but my probes c1w1 vs c1w8 (same bytes, width only) give ratio 1 vs 8 (logs/verify/PROV-02-verify-probes.log), so the width is the sole cause. The control genuinely shows no gap: hAssessed == h' == 0.6117162047939451 at width 1.
(c) PASS requires rc 0, four parsed floats, hA == dws*hB (1e-12 rel), dws*h' ~ hA (1e-5*dws), |hA-h'| >= 1e-5, dws > 1. Absent h' line or absent hAssessed -> Python ValueError -> FAIL (7c, 7d). Mutant (expect hA == hB) -> RESULT: FAIL exit 1 (STEP 3). Dead code at line 47; 'unitkeys' (lines 19-32) logged but NOT asserted and its hit list (bitsPerSymbol,bitsPerSymbolInferred) contradicts the PASS message's 'no unit or mode field' clause; the -vvv run's rc is not asserted (informational only).

